# Weekend Change Limits

Small, readable changes are easier to check than big clever ones.

## Before editing

- List the files you plan to create or change, with one line on why for each.
- If the list has more than 5 files, stop and propose a smaller first step.

## File-touch limits (per request)

- Change at most 5 files unless the human approves more.
- Create at most 3 new files unless the human approves more.
- Add no new dependency without asking first. Name the package and the reason.
- Do not rename, move, or reformat files that the task does not need.
- Do not create new top-level folders.
- Keep one concern per change. Unrelated fixes go in the "Later" list.

## Definition of done

A task is done only when all of these are true:

- The main flow works once, end to end, and you give the exact steps to check it.
- The project builds (or typechecks) without new errors or warnings you added.
- No secrets in code. New environment variables are added to `.env.example`.
- No placeholder logic is left in the main flow. Any stub is named in the summary.
- Your reply ends with a short summary in plain English:
  - What changed (files and one line each)
  - How to test it
  - What you did not do, and anything that still needs the human

If you cannot meet the definition of done, say which item is missing and why.
Do not report "done" or "everything works" without the steps to check it.
